      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Tiger-Seal is a 3/3 with vigilance but taps itself at the beginning of your upkeep, meaning it can't attack unless you draw a second card each turn to untap it. Fear of Missing Out is a 2/3 that provides card filtering (discard/draw) on ETB and has delirium synergy for extra combat phases. With only Island and Multiversal Passage as remaining land drops (no blue mana source beyond Spirebluff Canal already in play), casting Tiger-Seal uses the blue mana but results in a creature that will be tapped down most turns without reliable second-card-draw triggers. Fear of Missing Out would have been better as it provides immediate card selection (looting on ETB), can actually attack as a 2/3 without self-tapping restrictions, and contributes to delirium. The Tiger-Seal will likely just sit tapped doing nothing for several turns.",
